  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Multi-stakeholders capacities strengthened to stablishing a safe reporting mechanism for whistleblower protection</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Percentage of participants reporting increased understanding of gender-inclusive approaches to anti-corruption after completing the training modules, disaggregated by sex and age to measure differentiated learning outcomes.

Percentage of participants applying prosecution guidelines and anti-corruption measures in their work, one year after training, disaggregated by sex and age to assess differentiated application rates among men, women, and youth

Percentage of justice stakeholders (judicial personnel, law enforcement agencies, legal practitioners) who used anti-corruption guidelines, digital tools and reporting mechanisms in case management, investigation or prosecution24, disaggregated by sex and age.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2026"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2026-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2026-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="30"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">An Anti-corruption communication plan is developed and implemented.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Percentage of target citizens disaggregated by sex and age demonstrating increased awareness, enhanced knowledge, and engaged in implementing anti-corruption communication plan.

Percentage of trained CSOs, including women CSOs and journalists who have produced or implemented anti-corruption communication campaigns as part of the action plan.

Percentage of participants in advocacy and awareness sessions reporting an increased understanding and using of anti-corruption tools and mechanisms, disaggregated by sex and age to assess differentiated learning outcomes and engagement levels.

Percentage of participants demonstrating increased awareness of gender-based corruption issues, including sextortion, and understanding how to safely report such cases

Number of information, education and communications (IEC) materials developed

Percentage increase in public reporting of corruption cases after the implementation of the anti-corruption communication campaign, disaggregated by sex and age to assess engagement levels among men, women, and youth.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2026"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2028-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2028-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="40"></target>
     <actual value="0"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Institutional and legal framework for anti-corruption efforts are strengthened</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">Percentage of citizens, disaggregated by age and sex, reporting corruption cases via established mechanisms (e.g. e-platforms, hotlines, and whistleblower channels).</narrative>
